cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: report
title: "Wayfinding Architecture: An Architecture for Discoverable, Bounded, and Safe Change"
abstract: >-
  Software changes faster and more safely when every decision lives in one
  place you can find and every change has a clear scope. Wayfinding is an
  architectural approach that makes the ownership, impact, and scope of
  software changes explicit, discoverable, and enforceable, with an operating
  procedure for AI coding agents.
authors:
